    <summary>A free, skinnable task manager and system monitor, portable, no installer.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[TMOP shows what your computer is doing: how busy the processor, memory, disk, network and graphics card are, which programs are running, and much more. It runs on Windows, Linux and macOS, is free and open source (GPL-3.0), and needs no installer.

## Features

- Per-core CPU, memory, disk, network and graphics card, with engines where the system reports them.
- Processes with end task, suspend and priority; services, startup apps, installed apps and connections.
- Table columns you can put in any order; a Disk Space scan with a treemap; benchmarks; a flight recorder; and a Docker page.
- Skinnable: skins, palettes and fonts change how it looks. TMOP can take the place of Windows Task Manager (Ctrl+Shift+Esc).
- No telemetry. TMOP itself sends no data.

## Package notes

- This is a portable package. It downloads the official `TMOP-v0.15.0-windows-x64.zip` from the GitHub release, verifies its SHA256 and unpacks it into the package folder. The command `tmop` starts the program.
- Only the 64-bit Intel/AMD build is packaged. On Windows on ARM it runs through Windows' x64 emulation; the native ARM64 build is on the [releases page](https://github.com/tekikaito/tmop/releases).
- TMOP is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may warn the first time it starts.
- Settings are kept in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\TMOP`, so they survive upgrades and uninstalls.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/tekikaito/tmop/releases/tag/v0.15.0</releaseNotes>
